# Liveness SDK Rules for Windsurf

When implementing or modifying features involving @liveness/sdk and biometric face verification:

- Video Configuration: Video elements must include playsInline, autoPlay, and muted attributes.
- Hardware Cleanup: Always call sdk.stop(videoElement) and stop stream tracks (track.stop()) when components unmount.
- Asset Paths: Provide basePath pointing to /face_mesh/ and /mobilenet-v2/ binary assets or host them in public/.
- Active Challenges: Supported active challenges are BLINK, TURN_LEFT, TURN_RIGHT. Initial framing occurs during WAITING with distance guidance CLOSER / FURTHER.
- Client-Side Privacy: Only send the 1792-dimensional numerical descriptor vector to the server. Never stream raw camera video to backend.
- Biometric Matching: Use Cosine Similarity with default threshold >= 0.80.
- Webhooks: Always verify x-liveness-signature HMAC-SHA256 signatures against the raw body buffer (req.rawBody).
